{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your mobile data speed issues. First, I need to verify your account to provide technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Your current plan has a monthly data limit of 15GB, and you have already used 15.1GB this cycle. This is why your mobile data is extremely slow or not working—your data limit has been reached. You can either add more data (up to 2GB at $2.00 per GB) or change to a plan with a higher data limit. Would you like to refuel your data now, and if so, how many GB would you like to add (up to 2GB)?"
}

{
  "message": "2GB of data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. Your mobile data should now work again at normal speeds. If you still experience issues, please restart your phone to ensure the new data is applied. Let me know if you need any further assistance!"
}

{
  "message": "You're welcome! Please test your internet speed, and if it's not excellent or you experience any further issues, let me know. I'm here to help you troubleshoot and improve your mobile data experience."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. Let's troubleshoot your mobile data connection step by step. First, please check if Airplane Mode is enabled on your phone. To do this, please toggle Airplane Mode ON and then OFF again. This can help reset your phone's network connection. Let me know once you've done this, or if you need instructions on how to do it."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. Let's try to improve your connection. Please do the following steps:

1. Change your network mode preference to prioritize 4G/5G networks (instead of 2G).
2. Turn off Data Saver mode.

These changes can help you get a faster and more stable internet connection. Let me know once you've completed these steps or if you need instructions on how to do them."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please test your internet speed again now that your phone is connected to 5G with an excellent signal and Data Saver is off. This should provide you with the best possible mobile data speed. Let me know the results or if you need any further assistance!"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. Since you have an excellent 5G signal but still no internet access, the next step is to check your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings. Incorrect APN settings can prevent your phone from connecting to the internet. Please check your APN settings and let me know if you see any errors or if the MMSC URL is missing. If you're unsure how to check, I can guide you through the process."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking your APN settings. Since your APN and MMSC URL appear correct, let's try resetting your APN settings to default, as this can resolve hidden configuration issues. After resetting, please reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Let me know once you've completed these steps or if you need instructions on how to do them."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience and for following all the troubleshooting steps so far. Since you have an excellent 5G signal, correct APN settings, and have already reset and rebooted your device, but still have no internet connection, there may be a deeper technical issue with your line or account that I am unable to resolve directly. I will transfer you to a human agent who can further investigate and resolve this issue for you."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I’m here to help you get your mobile data working as well as possible! To start, I’ll guide you step by step. First, could you please provide your phone number or your full name and date of birth? This will help me identify your account and assist you better."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help improve your mobile data speed, I’ll guide you through a few steps. First, please check if Airplane Mode is turned off on your phone. \n\nCan you please turn Airplane Mode ON, wait a few seconds, and then turn it OFF again? This can help reset your network connection. Let me know once you’ve done this, and I’ll guide you to the next step."
}

{
  "message": "Great job! Turning Airplane Mode on and off will not affect your photos or any other data on your phone—it only resets your network connection.

Next, let’s make sure your phone is set to use the fastest available network. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred' if you see that option. This will help your phone connect to the best possible network for speed.

Let me know once you’ve done this, or if you need help finding this setting."
}

{
  "message": "No problem, I’ll guide you! Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred' on your phone. This will allow your phone to connect to the fastest available network and should improve your data speed.\n\nIf you see an option for 'Network Mode' or 'Preferred Network Type' in your phone’s settings, select it and choose '4G/5G Preferred.' Let me know once you’ve done this, or if you need more detailed steps for your specific phone model."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, if your phone says that data is disabled, you’ll need to turn your mobile data ON to use the internet. Please go to your phone’s settings and look for 'Mobile Data' or 'Cellular Data.' Make sure it is switched ON.\n\nOnce you’ve done that, let me know if you see the data symbol (like 4G or 5G) and if your internet is working. If you need help finding this setting, just let me know your phone’s make and model and I can give you more specific instructions."
}

{
  "message": "Perfect! Now that mobile data is ON and you see the 5G symbol, please try using the internet—open a website or an app that needs internet access to see if it’s working quickly. If it’s still slow or not working as expected, let me know, and I’ll help you with the next steps to improve your connection."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. Since you see the 5G symbol but still have no internet connection, there may be an issue with your phone’s data settings. Let’s try resetting your phone’s APN (Access Point Name) settings, which control how your phone connects to the internet. 

Please go to your phone’s settings, find the 'Mobile Network' or 'Cellular Network' section, and look for 'Access Point Names' or 'APN.' There should be an option to reset these settings to default. After resetting, please restart (reboot) your phone. 

Let me know once you’ve done this, or if you need step-by-step instructions for your specific phone model."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please try using the internet again now—open a website or app that needs internet access. Resetting the APN settings and restarting your phone often fixes connection issues. Let me know if your internet is working now, or if you’re still having trouble. I’m here to help until we get this sorted out!"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. I checked your account, and your line is active and you still have data left in your plan for this billing cycle, so you should be able to use mobile data.

Since everything looks correct on your account and you see the 5G symbol with excellent signal, but you still have no internet, there may be a more complex technical issue.

Before I escalate this, could you please confirm if you are using a VPN (Virtual Private Network) on your phone? Sometimes, a VPN can block or slow down your internet connection. If you are, please try disconnecting it and test your internet again. Let me know what you find, and I’ll continue helping you."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. Since you are not using a VPN and all your settings look correct, let's try one more thing: please check if Data Saver mode is turned ON. Data Saver can sometimes block internet access for some apps.\n\nGo to your phone's settings, look for 'Data Saver' or 'Data Usage,' and make sure Data Saver is turned OFF. After you do this, try using the internet again and let me know if it works. If it still doesn't work, I will escalate your issue for further technical support."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help you with your MMS issue, I’ll need to check a few settings on your phone. First, please check your network mode and make sure it is set to prefer 4G or 5G networks, as MMS may not work properly on 2G. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred' and let me know once you’ve done that."
}

{
  "message": "Great, thank you. Next, please make sure that your mobile data is turned ON, as MMS messages require mobile data to send and receive. Please toggle your mobile data ON and let me know once you have done this."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that mobile data is ON. I have now enabled data roaming on your line, which can help with MMS delivery in some cases. Please try sending an MMS message again. If it still does not work, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messages are now working! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for verifying your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need you to perform a few quick checks and actions on your phone. First, can you confirm if you are able to make regular calls and use mobile data (for example, browsing the web) on your phone right now?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the details. MMS requires at least a 3G network and a working data connection. Since your phone is currently on 2G and has no data, please change your network mode to prefer 4G/5G. On your phone, set the network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred'. Let me know once you’ve done this or if you need instructions."
}

{
  "message": "Great! The next step is to make sure data roaming is enabled on your phone, as this can help restore your data connection if you are outside your home network. Please go to your phone’s settings and turn on data roaming. Let me know once you’ve done this or if you need help finding the option."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for enabling data roaming. Please try sending an MMS message now and also check if your mobile data connection is working for browsing the web. Let me know if you are able to send MMS or if you are still experiencing issues."
}

{
  "message": "That’s great news! Yes, please try sending an MMS message to confirm that everything is working as expected. If the message goes through successfully, your issue should be resolved. If you encounter any further problems, let me know and I can assist you with additional troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "You're welcome! I'm glad to hear your MMS messages are working again. If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}
